{:edb/committed true :edb/basis-t 1455 :edb/replayed false :edb/tx-hash "55724de413d03eb9a35743cd714818d289b308f527d0f6f321f610c7af400592" :edb/db-before-t 1454 :edb/db-after-t 1455 :edb/tx-data [[13194139534767 50 #inst "2026-10-08T06:21:04.979Z" 13194139534767 true] [17592186054759 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308860 13194139534767 true] [17592186096628 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308847 13194139534767 true] [17592186115102 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308840 13194139534767 true] [17592186115206 1020 #edb/ref 17592186308856 13194139534767 true] [17592186308840 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308841 13194139534767 true] [17592186308840 1089 "q-120635" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308840 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045464 13194139534767 true] [17592186308840 1100 "Given that ${x}_{1}$ and ${x}_{2}$ are the solutions to the equation $3-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x$ for $-{180}^{∘}<x<{180}^{∘},$ what is the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2},$ rounded to the nearest integer?" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308840 1113 #uuid "34f30bac-93c7-5019-95f7-3ddbfb548336" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308840 1142 true 13194139534767 true] [17592186308840 1145 "First, we rearrange the equation and isolate $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}3-4\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =-2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x \\\\ -2\\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =-3 \\\\ \\operatorname{cot}⁡x & =\\frac{3}{2}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\operatorname{cot}⁡x=\\frac{1}{\\operatorname{tan}⁡x}.$ Therefore, the given equation is equivalent to\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{tan}⁡x=\\frac{2}{3}.\n$$\n\nNow, we find the principal value:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x=\\text{arctan}(\\frac{2}{3})=(33.690\\,0…)^{∘}≈{33.690}^{∘}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSince ${33.690}^{∘}$ lies inside the given domain, our first solution is ${x}_{1}={33.690}^{∘}.$\n\nTo generate more solutions, we add and subtract integer multiples of ${180}^{∘}.$ Hence,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}_{2}=-{180}^{∘}+{33.690}^{∘}=-{146.310}^{∘}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nSo, the solutions are $x=-{146.310}^{∘},\\,{33.690}^{∘}.$\n\nFinally, the numerical value of ${x}_{1}\\cdot {x}_{2}$ is \n\n$$\n(-146.310)\\cdot 33.690≈-4\\,929\n$$\n\nrounded to the nearest integer." 13194139534767 true] [17592186308841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308842 13194139534767 true] [17592186308841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308843 13194139534767 true] [17592186308841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308844 13194139534767 true] [17592186308841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308845 13194139534767 true] [17592186308841 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308846 13194139534767 true] [17592186308841 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045450 13194139534767 true] [17592186308841 1041 "selection" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308841 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308845 13194139534767 true] [17592186308841 1110 #uuid "81150a3d-4af3-556e-8c7a-50ba848986b2" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308842 1034 "-7\\,897" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308842 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308842 1111 #uuid "9e25b4b2-22f4-5ecd-bdda-279c63492cb8" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308843 1034 "-6\\,346" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308843 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308843 1111 #uuid "48f4fc96-edb1-5301-a879-d8330c8a7362" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308844 1034 "-8\\,124" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308844 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308844 1111 #uuid "b9c26c9a-34b7-58d4-9bca-3d74b372c53a" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308845 1034 "-4\\,929" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308845 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308845 1111 #uuid "21acaee4-f32d-5f2a-8fc2-54c8728903f4" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308846 1034 "-7\\,235" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308846 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308846 1111 #uuid "aba11855-a554-50d0-9968-f9a7f8be3735" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308847 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308848 13194139534767 true] [17592186308847 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308850 13194139534767 true] [17592186308847 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308852 13194139534767 true] [17592186308847 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308854 13194139534767 true] [17592186308847 1089 "q-251446" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308847 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534767 true] [17592186308847 1100 "**From left to right**, the points of intersection of the parabola ${x}^{2}=4(y+\\frac{1}{2})$ with the $x$-axis are $A$ and $B.$ Find the **exact** coordinates of $A$ and $B.$\n\n$A(${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$)\\,$ and $\\,B(${{field-3}}$,$\n{{field-4}}$)$" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308847 1113 #uuid "5c1bda76-f90d-562c-b15f-d7fb64f98b44" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308847 1145 "When the parabola intersects the $x$-axis, we must have $y=0.$ So, we set $y=0$ and solve the resulting equation for $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2} & =4(0+\\frac{1}{2}) \\\\ {x}^{2} & =2 \\\\ x & =\\pm \\sqrt{2}\\text{ }\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the coordinates of the intersection points, from left to right, are $(-\\sqrt{2},0)$ and $(\\sqrt{2},0).$" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308848 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308849 13194139534767 true] [17592186308848 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534767 true] [17592186308848 1041 "field-1" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308848 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308849 13194139534767 true] [17592186308848 1110 #uuid "5db4c15c-6db2-5378-bd97-c6a561fcf818" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308849 1034 "-\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308849 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308849 1111 #uuid "d02e939d-59c6-5a31-96f6-14ee3057436e" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308850 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308851 13194139534767 true] [17592186308850 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534767 true] [17592186308850 1041 "field-2" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308850 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308851 13194139534767 true] [17592186308850 1110 #uuid "14d38cc9-4dac-509d-9710-8e52178c1b6b" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308851 1034 "0" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308851 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308851 1111 #uuid "8932798f-16d9-5a0d-9525-969c5fa41a7c" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308852 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308853 13194139534767 true] [17592186308852 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534767 true] [17592186308852 1041 "field-3" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308852 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308853 13194139534767 true] [17592186308852 1110 #uuid "294f81e3-77a5-5e56-b619-5941fd3a14ac" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308853 1034 "\\sqrt{2}" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308853 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308853 1111 #uuid "f33b269b-2d26-5ae9-b02f-010e6ec8c749" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308854 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308855 13194139534767 true] [17592186308854 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534767 true] [17592186308854 1041 "field-4" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308854 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308855 13194139534767 true] [17592186308854 1110 #uuid "192c1a57-a3b9-593d-9f8f-1ea3af702df7" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308855 1034 "0" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308855 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308855 1111 #uuid "ac1faf61-5f85-5150-a55a-f457484b60fb" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308856 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308857 13194139534767 true] [17592186308856 1089 "q-281343" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308856 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045463 13194139534767 true] [17592186308856 1100 "A quadratic equation with real coefficients has a complex root $x=2+5\\text{i}.$ Given that the coefficient of ${x}^{2}$ in the equation is $1,$ find the equation. Write your answer in the form $a{x}^{2}+bx+c=0,$ where $a,$ $b,$ and $c$ are real constants.\n\n{{field-1}}$=0$" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308856 1113 #uuid "387c5ba6-af83-553b-9db1-67f720d2ad8d" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308856 1145 "Since the quadratic equation has real coefficients and $x=2+5\\text{i}$ is a root, we know that its complex conjugate $x=2-5\\text{i}$ is also a root. Therefore, using the zero product property, we can write a quadratic equation with the required roots as follows:\n\n$$\n(x-(2+5\\text{i}))(x-(2-5\\text{i}))=0\n$$\n\nBy expanding the parentheses, we can write the equation in standard form as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-x(2+5\\text{i})-x(2-5\\text{i})+(2+5\\text{i})(2-5\\text{i}) & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-2x-\\cancel{5x\\text{i}}-2x+\\cancel{5x\\text{i}}+4-25{\\text{i}}^{2} & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+4+25 & =0 \\\\ {x}^{2}-4x+29 & =0\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308857 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308858 13194139534767 true] [17592186308857 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308859 13194139534767 true] [17592186308857 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534767 true] [17592186308857 1041 "field-1" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308857 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308858 13194139534767 true] [17592186308857 1110 #uuid "24fad0c8-a8f5-5710-adde-1d8e174aafd0" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308858 1034 "x^2-4x+29" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308858 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308858 1111 #uuid "b90d648d-171f-51c2-97b0-752a3130e8ed" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308859 1034 "x^2-4x-21" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308859 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308859 1111 #uuid "35b7eb22-1da7-567a-b313-335e0fde6de2" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308860 1017 #edb/ref 17592186308861 13194139534767 true] [17592186308860 1089 "q-341918" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308860 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139534767 true] [17592186308860 1100 "Find the slope $m$ of the tangent at the point $(9,\\,4)$ for the curve $\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}=1.$\n\n$m=$\n{{field-1}}" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308860 1113 #uuid "58748e15-69f9-5abe-94c4-9c4bd5de4ccf" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308860 1145 "To find the slope at a point, we use implicit differentiation to calculate the derivative of the curve, assuming that $y=y(x).$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(\\sqrt{x}-\\sqrt{y}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}({x}^{1/2}-{y}^{1/2}) & =\\frac{\\text{d}}{\\text{d}x}(1) \\\\ \\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2}-\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =0 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2}{y}^{-1/2}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =-\\frac{1}{2}{x}^{-1/2} \\\\ -\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}}(\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}) & =-\\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{x}} \\\\ \\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x} & =\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{\\sqrt{x}}\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe slope of the tangent at the point $(9,\\,4)$ is then given by\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}m & ={\\frac{\\text{d}y}{\\text{d}x}|}_{(9,\\,4)} \\\\  & ={(\\frac{\\sqrt{y}}{\\sqrt{x}})|}_{(9,\\,4)} \\\\  & =\\frac{\\sqrt{4}}{\\sqrt{9}} \\\\  & =\\frac{2}{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308861 1000 #edb/ref 17592186308862 13194139534767 true] [17592186308861 1040 #edb/ref 17592186045449 13194139534767 true] [17592186308861 1041 "field-1" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308861 1104 #edb/ref 17592186308862 13194139534767 true] [17592186308861 1110 #uuid "44a1e65b-ed67-5754-af82-d0f5f3843575" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308862 1034 "\\frac{2}{3}" 13194139534767 true] [17592186308862 1103 #edb/ref 17592186045453 13194139534767 true] [17592186308862 1111 #uuid "5f96ca09-8ca1-5d53-bd11-868ef46d5e0a" 13194139534767 true]] :edb/tempids {"q-120635" 17592186308840 "q-120635/selection" 17592186308841 "q-120635/selection/a0606a0cdebd02311c23d8c017df9a506d8191ddb88f3bdf51fd6abb09218e89" 17592186308842 "q-120635/selection/b9e00ab3379bec21c45dbffdf81a5557166893ec01b6fa37cf08762ec0e97178" 17592186308843 "q-120635/selection/c66592ef9d82a82bc596d46943042a7623b2b133826f608359596f34dcd3777c" 17592186308844 "q-120635/selection/c9a21686d64b2acb6867e68200ef0e858a5ab7d2f9c929f4eb9e632f242d8d0d" 17592186308845 "q-120635/selection/f61408d6cec69744ff85fd904a6bc46c66cd7853ad9182259242270f95e97e1b" 17592186308846 "q-251446" 17592186308847 "q-251446/field-1" 17592186308848 "q-251446/field-1/df4ef3a75f6d71027299791921d9536d50890079e16123ff435f8ed8ac6150b0" 1